# Governance, not code.
#
# Four paths, deliberately. The builder must not be its own approver, but it
# also must not need an approver to do ordinary work — so what is owned here is
# only what defines or enforces the architecture, never what builds on it.
#
# Everything else about enforcement is covered indirectly and on purpose:
# scripts/contract-integrity.mjs records the hash, the check count and the CI
# invocation of every contract script in governance/idui-contract.json, so a
# gate cannot be edited, weakened or dropped from CI without a visible diff to
# the registry below. One reviewed file instead of ten owned ones, and it
# catches more than owning the scripts would.
#
# This file is documentation until the branch ruleset enforces it. Until then
# the gates are enforced but NOT agent-closed, and are described that way.

/governance/**                          @dechadae
/.github/workflows/**                   @dechadae
/scripts/ui-centralization-budget.json  @dechadae
/CODEOWNERS                             @dechadae
